In article <5674@cbnewsh.ATT.COM> stas@cbnewsh.ATT.COM (Stan Ciesielski) writes:
>get it to look right on my PC.  I have a Tandy 1000a
>with CM-4 color monitor. I noticed that there's a termcap.cnf
>	    <-J2+k3

That is the mark of control characters that are trying to be translated
to your screen.  You need to add "device=ansi.sys" to your config.sys
file if you have the ansi.sys file.  nansi.sys is even better
and is the only one that I have seen that truly works with larn.


